nose_adares_t2_local_geometry.py\", \"sha256\": \"c69d588069296f979f78a7b796e2d20313df53e4738adeaae487a374d1cc9688\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T2_geometry_train64_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"c9464e5b9b7b874b8e06bfb0c2031967142624d7369fd2d9c1c9438a8074a02e\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-T1-T2_diagnosis_20260926-235700.md\", \"sha256\": \"f0e1de67bb97a83fc32ec517527caad06dd2398d69a0beb00db92caf7aae2bd3\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-U1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not train or fuse mask-conditioned 3D/2D agreement: oracle higher in 148/388 train64 material errors versus outside-mask control 207/388; standalone mIoU 0.09220 versus B4 0.82256. Reopen only with a distinct inference-valid causal mechanism and prospective controls, not a feature or weight scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_u1_cross_modal_agreement.py\", \"sha256\": \"09d9771a5224a09a4772dc2aaecc5abd2ea004ea1bb70869296dce7334b14a12\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1_cross_modal_train64_20260927.json\", \"sha256\": \"34593792a610e49728a6295b851cdc1ae8ca7fbaded522ec92e7c3101d378730\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1-U2_diagnosis_20260927-010000.md\", \"sha256\": \"5e9188afbd10e366e39e08e5adddfef398b98bc7949917b1eef849f5a77a1826\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-U2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not train or scan max-token mask-language compatibility: oracle higher in 179/388 train64 errors versus shifted-language control 182/388; standalone mIoU 0.00814 versus B4 0.82256. Reopen only with new independent token-specific evidence and a native matched control.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_u2_token_mask_agreement.py\", \"sha256\": \"34047e0c9107cd96d8fff8fbd5498c52cba642431b4092694bd93de5c30a2274\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U2_token_mask_train64_20260927.json\", \"sha256\": \"93769e807a72fcf80e7f8cdde81f01d9866d545cc4e676d73593bf154b81f0f3\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1-U2_diagnosis_20260927-010000.md\", \"sha256\": \"5e9188afbd10e366e39e08e5adddfef398b98bc7949917b1eef849f5a77a1826\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_cycle\": {\n    \"at\": \"2026-09-27T01:00:00+08:00\",\n    \"candidate_budget\": 2,\n    \"admitted\": 0,\n    \"attempted_ids\": [\"AdaRES-U1\", \"AdaRES-U2\"],\n    \"stop_reason\": \"independent_routes_exhausted\",\n    \"stop_detail\": \"U1 cross-modal inside agreement 0.09220 mIoU and U2 token-resolved compatibility 0.00814 versus B4 0.82256 on fixed train64; paired error ordering fails outside-mask and shifted-language controls respectively. Both fail diagnosis/control before backward/resource gates. No further distinct evidence-backed executable route identified in this bounded cycle; no global exhaustion claim.\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1_cross_modal_train64_20260927.json\", \"sha256\": \"34593792a610e49728a6295b851cdc1ae8ca7fbaded522ec92e7c3101d378730\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U2_token_mask_train64_20260927.json\", \"sha256\": \"93769e807a72fcf80e7f8cdde81f01d9866d545cc4e676d73593bf154b81f0f3\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1-U2_diagnosis_20260927-010000.md\", \"sha256\": \"5e9188afbd10e366e39e08e5adddfef398b98bc7949917b1eef849f5a77a1826\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260927-010000.md\", \"sha256\": \"e7c251913f862edfad365b0af4a63a7ac426235ffc7d86616445842314902cba\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260927-010000.md\", \"sha256\": \"070e854efe022bbdca92bdc9208f98ea34d69b16a11e066e15eb5fa4e1eb9c29\"}\n    ],\n    \"resume_condition\": \"Next capacity-gap tick: seek independently justified inference-available metric-aligned confidence evidence beyond U1/U2 and prior rejected routes; predeclare paired native training controls and pass all six gates before admission. Reconcile any monitor/goal event first.\"\n  },\n  \"migration_notes\": \"AdaRES did not previously have research work tracking; B4 and B5 are the first explicit queued records.\"\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content pipeline/decisions/20260927-010053_route_change.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1-U2_diagnosis_20260927-010000.md -Raw; Get-Content pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260927-010000.md -Raw'","aggregated_output":"# AdaRES_project 决策记录\n\n- **时间**: 2026-09-27 01:00:52\n- **类型**: route_change\n- **问题**: U1/U2 fixed native train64: admit either vacant server-2 slot?\n- **决策**: Reject cross-modal U1 and token-mask U2; leave server-2 GPU0/1 unqueued\n- **依据**: U1 oracle ordering 148/388 vs outside 207/388 and mIoU 0.09220; U2 179/388 vs shifted 182/388 and mIoU 0.00814; B4 0.82256; diagnosis/controls fail\n- **证据**: pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-U1-U2_diagnosis_20260927-010000.md; pipeline/research_work.json\n\r\n# Fixed native diagnosis: U1 and U2\n\n2026-09-27 01:00 Asia/Shanghai. Prepared monitor and goal checks were not rerun. Server-2 GPU0, key SSH, B4-E30 best checkpoint, fixed first 64 ScanRefer training scenes (1660 expressions). Read-only inference, no validation tuning. Repeated forwards matched in both probes.\n\n## U1: Masked cross-modal agreement\n\nThe proposed signal compares pooled projected 3D and 2D features inside each predicted mask. Outside-mask and cyclically shifted 2D features are controls. Of 388 material B4 selection errors, the missed oracle had greater inside agreement in 148, outside agreement in 207, shifted agreement in 165. Agreement-only top-1 mIoU was 0.09220, versus B4 0.82256, outside-only 0.38530 and shifted-only 0.03072. This is neither discriminative nor superior to its controls. Inference peak reservation 3.60 GiB does not qualify training resources.\n\n## U2: Token-resolved mask-language compatibility\n\nThe proposed signal takes the maximum valid-token cosine match to the predicted mask's foreground-minus-background scene representation. A scene-shifted language match is the control. Of 388 material errors, oracle match was greater in 179, versus 182 with shifted language. Token-only mIoU was 0.00814 versus B4 0.82256 and shifted-only 0.01109. This does not establish expression-specific metric evidence. Inference peak reservation 3.56 GiB does not qualify training resources.\n\n## Gates\n\nReject U1 and U2 on diagnosis/control evidence. No candidate-specific native backward, training resource test, independent model/config, admission receipt, training sync, dispatch, or queue mutation. This is bounded exhaustion of these two routes, not a claim that all hypotheses are exhausted. Reconsider only on a prospectively specified inference-available mechanism with matched native controls and all six gates.\n\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-27 01:00 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Active 0/2, candidate budget 2. U1 tests mask-conditioned 3D/2D agreement; U2 tests token-resolved mask-language compatibility.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nFixed train64 B4 readout 0.82256. U1 standalone 0.09220 with only 148/388 error oracles higher, worse than outside-mask ordering 207/388. U2 standalone 0.00814 with 179/388, no better than shifted-language control 182/388.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nReject both directions at diagnosis/control gates. No training variant is justified. Raw paired JSON and source probes are archived; no full-run metric or novelty claim.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nOne targeted key-SSH GPU query found server-2 GPU0/1 at 0% and 1 MiB before read-only GPU0 probes. No post-probe occupancy claim. No queue assignment; server-6 excluded.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed train64 U1/U2 native inference diagnoses and controls; repeat mismatch 0.\n- [x] Archive raw JSON, scripts and hashes.\n- [ ] A future candidate must pass diagnosis, controls, native backward, resources, independence and goal constraints before implementation, receipt, sync and safe dispatch.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nU1 compares projected modalities not independently trained for alignment. U2's maximum-token match is nondiscriminative versus shifted language. Inference peaks are not training resource gates.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nNo tuning-only, seed-repeat, pure ablation, banned, failed-route or renamed duplicate admitted. No weight, token subset or threshold scan proposed.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded routes tested; no global exhaustion claim.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
